      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PRINCESS DOCKER (8) has a strong record this track and trip with four wins and two placings from seven starts. Comes off a (22.95) win last time, scoring by 5.5 lengths in a Grade 5 over 400m at this track. Rates a leading player. TIGER TAILS (1) had the drop on the lead early on but could only manage third, beaten 3 lengths (23.18) at this track in a Grade 5 over 400m. Has performed well from this box with a win and three minor placings to her name from six starts. Hard to beat again. ALEX KEEPING (7) had a tricky draw and ran well to finish third, beaten 1.5 lengths, (19.90) at Gunnedah. Hard to beat again. JAMAICA RUM (2) is a last start winner who rates one of the chances again.",
